This is the final project in the subject Anlogic and Digital Control. With some improvings the project was sednde to a congress and later to IEEE Xplore, the link of the paper will be post here.

The Project consist in a current control of the grid side in three phase inverter using a LCL filter. Using the rotaing frame (alpha-beta) the system has been decoupling in two separete systems, discretizate and include the unity step delay. 
To design the controller a resonant controller was applied, and focused in reduce of sesnsor numbers a full state observer was implementad, in order ti compensate the disturbance during parametric variations a distrubance observer in exact discrete method was introduced. To guarantee the robistess in all scenarios a genetic algorithm was introduced to calculate the sub-optimal gains for controller and observer. The choice of GA is comparing of the classical methodos using LMI's approach is the objective function taht can be describe the desired response of the system.
